name>Willems</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Significance of initial ST segment elevation and depression for the management of thrombolytic therapy in acute myocardial infarction</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>1990</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>1147</fpage><lpage>1158</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2119263</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-wjem-9-0040"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bush</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferguson</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Angelini</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Twelve-lead electrocardiographic evaluation of ischemia during percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty and its correlation with acute reocclusion</article-title><source>American Heart Journal</source><year>1991</year><volume>121</volume><fpage>1591</fpage><lpage>1599</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2035373</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-wjem-9-0040"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tamura</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mikuriya</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kataoka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Emergent coronary angiographic findings of patients with ST leads, or both, during anterior wall acute myocardial infarction</article-title><source>American Journal of Cardiology</source><year>1995</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>516</fpage><lpage>517</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7653456</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-wjem-9-0040"><label>10</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fesmire</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Brady</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Hahn</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Clinical Policy: Indications for reperfusion therapy in Emergency Department patients with suspected acute myocardial infarction</article-title><source>Annals of Emergency Medicine</source><year>2006</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>358</fpage><lpage>383</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16997672</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-wjem-9-0040"><label>11</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pope</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruthazer</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Beshansky</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Clinical features of emergency department patients presenting with symptoms of acute cardiac ischemia: a multicenter study</article-title><source>Journal of Thrombosis and Thrombolysis</source><year>1998</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10751787</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-wjem-9-0040"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Writing Committee Members</collab><person-group person-group-type="author"><etal/></person-group><article-title>ACC/AHA guidelines for the management of patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction &#x02013; executive summary: A report of the American College of Cardiology/American Heart Association Task Force on practice guidelines (writing committee to revise the 1999 guidelines for the management of patients with acute myocardial infarction)</article-title><source>Journal of the American College of Cardiology</source><year>2004</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>671</fpage><lpage>719</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15358045</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-wjem-9-0040" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Examples of J point determination</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="wjem-9-0040f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-wjem-9-0040" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>The ECG Baseline</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="wjem-9-0040f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-wjem-9-0040" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>ECG Entrance Criteria in Select Mega-Trials</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Study</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Publication Year</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Duration of Symptoms Required</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Maximum Time to Onset Prior to Presentation</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">EKG Change Requirements</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Other Requirements/Modifiers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ISIS - 1 (13)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1986</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">-----</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12 hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">None</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MI suspected by MD</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ISIS - 1 (14)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1988</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">-----</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">24 hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">None</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MI suspected by MD</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">GISSI - 2 (15)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1990</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">-----</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6 hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><list list-type="order"><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 1mm in any limb lead</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 2mm in any precordial lead</p></list-item></list></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ISIS - 3 (16)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1992</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">-----</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">-----</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">None</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MD thought there was a &#x0201c;clear&#x0201d; indication for Fibrinolytics</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">GUSTO (17)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1993</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20 min</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6 hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><list list-type="order"><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.1mV in 2 or more limb leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.2mV in 2 or more contiguous precordial leads</p></list-item></list></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">GUSTO III (18)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1997</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30 min</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6 hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><list list-type="order"><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 1mm in 2 or more limb leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 2mm in precordial leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>BBB</p></list-item></list></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ASSENT - 2 (19)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1999</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">-----</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6 hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><list list-type="order"><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.1mV in 2 or more limb leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.2mV in 2 or more contiguous precordial leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>LBBB</p></list-item></list></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">InTIME - II (20)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2000</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30 min</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6 hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><list list-type="order"><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.1mV in any 2 contiguous limb leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.2mV in any 2 contiguous precordial leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.2mV in V4R</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.2mV in 2 contiguous posterior leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>New or presumed new LBBB</p></list-item></list></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">ASSENT - 3 (21)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2001</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">-----</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><list list-type="order"><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.1mV in 2 or more limb leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>STE &#x0003e; 0.2mV in 2 or more contiguous precordial leads</p></list-item><list-item><p>LBBB</p></list-item></list></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">GUSTO V (22)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2001</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30 min</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6hr</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0201c;EKG criteria for STEMI or New LBBB&#x0201d; (with references to GUSTO, GUSTO III &#x00026; ASSENT &#x02013; 2)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-group></article>